L	Sentinel	Forerunner machines left behind to guard their installations, firing a continuous beam. Some carry shields. Once they ignored humanity; now they defend the rings against the Flood and anyone else in the way.|Unless the Sentinels are set against you (Options > Halo CE AI), they fight on your side: they keep with you like a Marine squad and answer your squad orders.
L	SentinelConstructor	A little Forerunner builder drone, made to weld and mend the installation, not to fight. Turned on intruders it still does what it knows: it darts at you out of nowhere, rams you, and burns at you with its cutting beam. It cannot take much punishment.
L	SentinelCrawler	A Forerunner machine that walks instead of flying, scuttling across the floor on its legs. It keeps a beam for range and lunges at anyone who gets close.|Model and design by Galap.
L	SentinelDragoon	A long, T-shaped Forerunner gunship with a heavy shield. It carries the Enforcer's needle cannon, raking an area with strings of hard-light bolts from range, and a heavy beam gun under its nose that burns at you in long bursts at the same time.|The Dragoon Ally answers to humans instead, whatever the Sentinels' allegiance is set to.|Model and design by Galap.
L	SentinelEliminator	A Sentinel built for the purge's hardest work: a shield bubble around its hull and a beam that burns far hotter than the common Sentinel's. When one turns up, the Forerunner machines have decided you are worth the effort.
L	SentinelEnforcer	A heavy Forerunner war machine that floats on hover jets. Two energy shields across its front stop anything fired from ahead; it answers with long strings of needle bolts from both arms, salvoes of homing hard-light rockets, and its claws for anyone who gets close. Flank it: its back and sides are bare.
L	SentinelGold	A Sentinel cast in gold, burning a cold blue beam instead of the usual one. Majors are tougher, and the Shielded models carry an energy shield that has to be stripped first.|Model and design by Galap.
L	SentinelInterceptor	A slim, fast attack drone that fires needle bolts as it swoops. It cannot take much punishment, so knock it out of the air before it closes in.|Model and design by Galap.
L	SentinelKnight	A Forerunner war machine of hard light, built around a burning core. A Knight fights with the weapon that forms its right forearm and the blade on its left, and when its shield fails it sinks into the ground in a flash of light and rises again somewhere else, often right beside you.
L	SentinelKnightCommander	A gold-plated Knight commander with a warm-burning core: the toughest of its kind, with a heavy shield.
L	SentinelKnightMajor	A seasoned Knight with a stronger shield and more armour.
L	SentinelKnightMinor	The common Knight, plated in grey, its core burning a cold colour.
L	SentinelLancer	A Forerunner burner. It flies in close and sprays fire across whatever it finds, which makes it deadly in tight corridors and easy prey at range.|Model and design by Galap.
L	SentinelMarauder	A cross-winged Forerunner raider with a standard beam. It is light and quick, meant to harass rather than hold a line.|Model and design by Galap.
L	SentinelOnyx	A dark Forerunner drone of a different make, compact and heavily shielded, with a blue beam. It is slow to kill and quick to punish anyone who stands in the open.|Model and design by Galap.
L	SentinelProtector	A light escort drone with the Enforcer's needle cannon. On its own it is no great threat, but its hard-light bolts add up fast when it flies with others.|Model and design by Galap.
L	SentinelSoldier	The heaviest of the new Forerunner guardians: a broad, armoured hull with a strong shield and three beams: its own, and one from a gun on either side of the hull, each firing on its own. It takes a sustained effort to bring one down, and it soaks up fire the whole while.|The Soldier Ally answers to humans instead, whatever the Sentinels' allegiance is set to.|Model and design by Galap.
L	SentinelWarden	A well-shielded guardian of the installation, built to hold ground. Its beam is the common Sentinel's; its staying power is not.|Model and design by Galap.
